    "gen": {
     "tool": "edge-tts",
     "voice": "en-US-SteffanNeural",
     "rate": "+0%",
     "text": "In nineteen oh nine, the Eiffel Tower was running out of time. It was built for the 1889 World's Fair in Paris. Gustave Eiffel's permit gave it just twenty years. After that, the city could tear it down. So Eiffel made it useful, backing experiments in a new technology: radio. Its great height made it a powerful antenna, valuable to the French military. In 1910, Paris renewed the permit. The tower was saved. Today it stands 330 metres tall. Not bad for a temporary structure."
    }
   }
